rows.body:
{{#sundayWriteup}}{{sundayDate}}

The Moon stays in Cancer through most of the day before entering Leo at 6:54 PM EDT. After a day of being more sensitive to your surroundings, familiar comforts, and the people you care about, the emotional tone becomes warmer and more expressive. You may want affection to be more obvious, appreciation to be spoken aloud, or a little more enthusiasm from the people around you. Leo can make emotions more expressive, but also more tender around being noticed or overlooked.{{/sundayWriteup}}

{{#mondayWriteup}}{{mondayDate}}

The Moon spends the entire day in Leo, bringing more attention to self-expression, recognition, and the things that make you feel like yourself. You may feel more aware of how you are being received, but the deeper question is what you want to create, say, wear, share, or enjoy because it feels true to you. Leo wants warmth, generosity, and somewhere for the heart to go. Spend time with the people who make it easy to be fully yourself, return to something creative you have neglected, or give your attention to what makes you feel more alive. You do not need an audience for it to matter. 

The upcoming New Moon is close, but you do not need to know your intentions yet. Let this part of the cycle be about finishing, resting, and noticing what still matters once the noise dies down. What keeps coming back to mind now may be worth carrying into the next lunar cycle.{{/mondayWriteup}}

{{#tuesdayWriteup}}{{tuesdayDate}}

The Moon stays in Leo for most of today and enters Virgo at 10:52 PM EDT. The emotional tone begins to shift late tonight. Under Leo, you may have been more focused on what excites you, what you want to express, or what feels worth putting more of yourself into. As the Moon moves into Virgo, that enthusiasm becomes easier to work with. You may start seeing the next useful step, the small adjustment that would make something easier, or the detail that helps an idea come together. Because the change happens so late, you may notice it more clearly tomorrow.{{/tuesdayWriteup}}

{{#wednesdayWriteup}}{{wednesdayDate}}

The urge to fix everything can become its own source of exhaustion. Under a Virgo Moon, you may notice every loose end, every small mistake, and every place where reality falls short of the version you had in mind. That discernment is useful, but not everything you notice needs correcting.

This is a good time to organize what has become cumbersome, return to routines that help your body feel better, or make one practical change that genuinely improves your day. The point is not to perfect yourself. It is to make life work better. Leave some things unfinished. Let good enough be enough where it can be. You are allowed to improve something without treating yourself like the problem.{{/wednesdayWriteup}}

{{#thursdayWriteup}}{{thursdayDate}}

The Moon spends the entire day in Virgo before it enters {{openingSeasonSign}} tomorrow. Emotionally, Virgo can make you more aware of what feels unfinished, inefficient, or slightly off. A small mistake may bother you more than usual, and it can be tempting to keep adjusting things until everything feels under control. You may be more aware of what feels off today, but noticing a problem does not mean you have to fix it immediately.{{/thursdayWriteup}}

{{#fridayWriteup}}{{fridayDate}}

Once the Moon enters Libra, focus shifts from the mechanics of the task to the dynamics between people. Precision gives way to perspective. You begin to notice the subtle tone, the timing, and if the weight in the room is being shared evenly. Libra energy reminds us that harmony is an active choice, not a passive state. Right now, you are being invited to notice if balance has slipped, especially if one person is quietly making all the compromises. Make the adjustment that restores fairness. Clear the air, name what feels off, and put things back on equal footing. Connection rarely thrives in quiet resentment. More often, it deepens when you work together to bring things back into balance.{{/fridayWriteup}}

{{#saturdayWriteup}}{{saturdayDate}}

The {{openingSeasonSign}} New Moon opens a new cycle around what you choose and what you want more of. You may look at something you have been accepting out of habit and realize you would choose differently now. Maybe you want more time for something you genuinely enjoy, a different way of spending your attention, or fewer commitments that leave you wondering why you agreed in the first place. Let your New Moon intentions come from what you would choose differently if you were starting from where you are now.

